WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 11.13 · Fundraising, Revenue & Sustainable Business Models
Social enterprise and hybrid revenue models

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Show where impact happens in your revenue model, and protect it from drift.

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.600
1. Name your model: employment, service, intermediary, cross-subsidy or cooperative.

4
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.200
2. Measure impact and margin together, not separately.

5
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:22.200
3. Write safeguards: purpose clause, red lines, agreements between entities.

6
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:23.800
An example: Pan del Barrio (Social enterprise · company, Peru)

7
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:31.000
“Pan del Barrio: customers buy bread at market prices; the impact is 12 paid trainees a year, protected by the bylaws.”

8
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.400
You describe your revenue model and the safeguards around it.

9
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.400
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

10
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:42.000
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
